   "text": {
    "L1": "A bar graph shows numbers with bars. Read the scale before reading a bar.",
    "L2": "Here is a myth: a wider bar means more. Not true—the height gives the value, while width does not matter.",
    "L3": "This scale goes up in fives. So each step is 5, not 1.",
    "L4": "A bar reaching 25 shows 25. If it stops halfway between two marks, read the number halfway between them.",
    "L5": "To compare two bars, read both values first. Then subtract the smaller from the bigger.",
    "L6": "In the kite example, Tuesday has 40 and Monday has 25. Forty minus twenty-five is 15, so Tuesday has 15 more.",
    "L7": "Now check your reading. Which bar shows the larger number: Asha's 12 or Bilal's 8?"
   },
